{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186482565 "Let $X$ be a random variable with the probability density function shown below. What is the mode of $X?$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}3{e}^{-3x},\\, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0,\\, & x<0\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186482570 "Find the median of the random variable $X$ if the cumulative distribution function of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0, \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{144}, & 0\\le x\\le 12, \\\\ 1, & x>12.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186482571 "Find, to three decimal places, the interquartile range of the random variable $X$ if the cumulative distribution function of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1, \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}-1}{8}, & 1\\le x\\le 3, \\\\ 1, & x>3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186482575 "Find the median of the random variable $X$ if the probability density function of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<1, \\\\ \\frac{6}{{x}^{7}},\\, & x\\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186482584 "Let $D$ be a finite region enclosed by the curves $y=2{x}^{2}+1$ and $y=3.$ If $R=[-1,1]\\times [1,3],$ and\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following could be the definition of $f(x,y)?$\n\nI. $$\n\\displaystyle \\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y, & (x,y)\\in D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nII. $$\n\\displaystyle \\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIII. $$\n\\displaystyle \\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡y, & (x,y)\\in R∖D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in D\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186482588 "Let $X$ be a random variable with the probability density function shown below. What is the mode of $X?$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{(1+x)^{2}},\\, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186482591 "Find the median of 